1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,100
When you watch TV, brighten the
room and sit back a little, okay?

2
00:00:18,920 --> 00:00:24,380
Like someone is calling you,
the afternoon after the rain.

3
00:00:25,540 --> 00:00:31,040
Walking while looking back,
led by the hand by Gacha.

4
00:00:32,060 --> 00:00:38,220
That strange feeling I felt back then.

5
00:00:38,880 --> 00:00:43,460
So, on the tiles of the arcade street,

6
00:00:43,460 --> 00:00:49,220
I walked only on the black ones.

7
00:00:51,780 --> 00:00:57,380
Everyone was a child once,
but they've all forgotten.

8
00:00:58,540 --> 00:01:04,840
Politicians with their self-important faces,
and aunties with blue eyeshadow too.

9
00:01:05,360 --> 00:01:10,420
Go on, turn at that corner.

10
00:01:11,500 --> 00:01:15,600
You can meet everyone, everyone.

11
00:01:15,600 --> 00:01:20,380
Over there is Kameari.

12
00:01:21,560 --> 00:01:24,000
Well, surely it's Kameari.

13
00:01:24,440 --> 00:01:28,800
Everyone, come on, to our town.

14
00:01:29,760 --> 00:01:30,320
Thank you.

15
00:01:33,500 --> 00:01:36,520
The great showdown of
Odoroki Momo and Onijima!

16
00:01:40,280 --> 00:01:42,540
Morning.

17
00:01:43,020 --> 00:01:45,260
Good morning.

18
00:01:45,260 --> 00:01:46,440
Good morning.

19
00:01:46,440 --> 00:01:49,240
What is it,
did you drop your contact lens or something?

20
00:01:49,240 --> 00:01:51,660
We're looking for the spine of number 52.

21
00:01:52,560 --> 00:01:53,360
What's that supposed to be?

22
00:01:55,100 --> 00:01:56,460
It's a dinosaur model.

23
00:01:56,460 --> 00:01:57,980
One piece is missing.

24
00:01:57,980 --> 00:01:58,820
A model?

25
00:01:59,040 --> 00:02:01,500
You two, playing with this
kind of thing during work hours!

26
00:02:01,500 --> 00:02:03,700
Ryo... Ryotsu.

27
00:02:03,700 --> 00:02:04,820
Chief, just keep going.

28
00:02:05,200 --> 00:02:06,640
Found it, here it is.

29
00:02:06,640 --> 00:02:09,020
This is the 52nd vertebra.

30
00:02:09,920 --> 00:02:12,420
With this, the Brontosaurus is complete.

31
00:02:13,440 --> 00:02:15,640
Don't make things like
that during work hours.

32
00:02:15,640 --> 00:02:20,960
Chief, I'm making it for an elementary school as a teaching material,
you know.

33
00:02:20,960 --> 00:02:22,000
What kind of teaching material?

34
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:25,600
It's a precision model with 148 parts,
after all.

35
00:02:25,600 --> 00:02:27,600
An amateur could never build it.

36
00:02:27,600 --> 00:02:30,040
It's like a jigsaw puzzle.

37
00:02:30,040 --> 00:02:34,160
Assembling it accurately is even harder than a jigsaw,
you know.

38
00:02:34,160 --> 00:02:35,900
And what's more, Chief.

39
00:02:35,900 --> 00:02:40,300
This morning, while I was cutting the parts off the sprues,
painting them, and letting them dry,

40
00:02:47,400 --> 00:02:55,240
The Stegosaurus, Brontosaurus, and Plesiosaurus
bones have all gotten mixed up together.

41
00:02:55,820 --> 00:02:58,580
It's practically like being an
archaeologist doing an excavation.

42
00:02:58,580 --> 00:03:01,720
We have to judge each bone
one by one as we look at it.

43
00:03:02,640 --> 00:03:04,420
All the bones look the same.

44
00:03:05,980 --> 00:03:15,160
You look at them and reconstruct the bones correctly.
He won't do any real work, but he's diligent when it comes to this sort of thing. When it comes to skeletons, I'm a meticulous man.

45
00:03:15,160 --> 00:03:23,840
We've got a notice from Tokyo Metropolitan Government about your resident tax payment.
Honestly, where's the meticulousness? Isn't it deducted automatically from your salary?

46
00:03:23,840 --> 00:03:31,300
Only this one I've been dodging for five years, paying it personally.
I figured that with Governor Ishihara in office now, they'd let it slide.

47
00:03:31,680 --> 00:03:35,500
As if that would happen! It's a duty of every resident.
Now, make sure you pay it properly.

48
00:03:35,500 --> 00:03:36,060
Yeah, yeah.

49
00:03:36,800 --> 00:03:43,660
Senpai, Nakagawa Enterprises is holding a dinosaur exhibition soon.
Do you want to go see it?

50
00:03:44,360 --> 00:03:45,980
Really? I'm going, I'm going!

51
00:03:45,980 --> 00:03:47,820
Pay your resident tax first, then go.

52
00:03:47,820 --> 00:03:49,680
Yeah, yeah, I get it.

53
00:03:49,680 --> 00:03:52,580
Honestly, I don't want to be
lectured by people from Chiba.

54
00:03:52,580 --> 00:03:53,640
Did you say something?

55
00:03:53,640 --> 00:03:58,240
No, nothing at all.
Officer Ryotsu, I'm heading out on patrol.

56
00:04:01,240 --> 00:04:03,160
Honestly, that idiot.

57
00:04:20,740 --> 00:04:22,940
Yeah, the real thing really is different.

58
00:04:22,940 --> 00:04:24,680
I'd really love to have one.

59
00:04:24,680 --> 00:04:26,220
That's impossible.

60
00:04:26,220 --> 00:04:28,600
I'm not saying I want this one.

61
00:04:28,600 --> 00:04:30,220
I want the mold.

62
00:04:30,220 --> 00:04:30,680
Mold?

63
00:04:30,920 --> 00:04:31,720
Yeah, the mold.

64
00:04:31,720 --> 00:04:34,220
With your cooperation, it's possible.

65
00:04:34,220 --> 00:04:35,360
Come here, let me whisper something.

66
00:04:45,600 --> 00:04:46,560
Hey!

67
00:04:46,560 --> 00:04:47,900
Yosh, here we go!

68
00:04:47,900 --> 00:04:51,120
Senpai, whatever you do, don't break it!

69
00:04:51,120 --> 00:04:53,120
Don't worry, I've got it.

70
00:04:53,640 --> 00:04:56,160
What on earth are you going
to do with a mold of a bone?

71
00:04:56,840 --> 00:04:58,720
Apparently he wants to make an exact copy.

72
00:04:59,140 --> 00:05:01,540
Once he makes up his mind,
he won't back down.

73
00:05:02,180 --> 00:05:03,280
How frightening.

74
00:05:03,280 --> 00:05:05,480
That's the end of the Brontosaurus.

75
00:05:05,480 --> 00:05:06,820
Well then, let's head home.

76
00:05:06,820 --> 00:05:09,380
What are you talking about?
We're just getting started.

77
00:05:10,120 --> 00:05:11,380
You're still going to keep going?

78
00:05:11,460 --> 00:05:13,060
Next up is the Tyrannosaurus.

79
00:05:14,980 --> 00:05:18,180
We'll never get another chance
to take molds from the real thing.

80
00:05:18,180 --> 00:05:20,380
I'm going to take every
one while I have this chance.

81
00:05:22,820 --> 00:05:25,940
Coming here every night,
I'm hooked right down to the bone marrow.

82
00:05:33,500 --> 00:05:35,320
It's been a while since I had a day off.

83
00:05:35,320 --> 00:05:37,600
Maybe I'll go on a date with Nana today.

84
00:05:46,380 --> 00:05:47,480
Honda-san

85
00:05:48,540 --> 00:05:50,140
What's going on first thing in the morning?

86
00:05:51,300 --> 00:05:54,760
In the yard,
kaju kaju kaju kaju kaju kaju kaju

87
00:05:54,760 --> 00:05:58,280
Ryo-san is assembling the dinosaur skeleton.

88
00:05:58,280 --> 00:05:59,980
The senpai?

89
00:06:02,060 --> 00:06:05,460
I really wanted it as an
object for this Ryo's yard.

90
00:06:06,400 --> 00:06:08,900
This much space can display
five or six of them, right?

91
00:06:09,360 --> 00:06:11,340
I see, that's so like you, senpai.

92
00:06:12,380 --> 00:06:15,060
Shonda, you're free today, right?
Help me out.

93
00:06:15,060 --> 00:06:18,460
No, I was thinking of going
on a date with Nana-chan today.

94
00:06:19,080 --> 00:06:19,969
Hey, Honda.

95
00:06:20,019 --> 00:06:24,560
Who was it that helped you
start dating Nana Otohime?

96
00:06:25,040 --> 00:06:26,740
Well...

97
00:06:26,880 --> 00:06:32,840
Who was it that always comforted
you when you kept getting dumped?

98
00:06:33,120 --> 00:06:34,120
Senpai.

99
00:06:34,540 --> 00:06:40,020
Once people get happy, they forget
all about the old days, don't they.

100
00:06:40,120 --> 00:06:43,620
Understood. I'll help. Let me help you.

101
00:06:45,060 --> 00:06:47,097
Sorry about this, Honda. Well then,

102
00:06:47,147 --> 00:06:49,480
bring me that biggest bone over there.

103
00:06:50,640 --> 00:06:53,940
Ugh, no way. Me alone with a bone this big?

104
00:06:54,120 --> 00:06:55,920
Big as you are, what are you going on about?

105
00:06:57,140 --> 00:07:00,060
It's lighter than it looks.

106
00:07:00,620 --> 00:07:03,580
It's lightweight plastic and hollow inside,
after all.

107
00:07:04,200 --> 00:07:04,520
I see.

108
00:07:05,260 --> 00:07:07,654
Okay, set it down gently.

109
00:07:07,704 --> 00:07:10,800
Put this on top and hold it steady.

110
00:07:18,320 --> 00:07:20,180
You're really something, Ryotsu.

111
00:07:20,180 --> 00:07:25,580
I'm a specialist at making models,
after all.

112
00:07:25,580 --> 00:07:28,340
Ryo-san,
can I bring a friend over to see it?

113
00:07:28,340 --> 00:07:30,140
Bring as many as you like.

114
00:07:30,140 --> 00:07:31,760
Yeah, right.

115
00:07:33,140 --> 00:07:35,240
The kids will be thrilled, won't they?

116
00:07:35,240 --> 00:07:39,700
Ryotsu, you're not planning to
make money off this, are you?

117
00:07:39,700 --> 00:07:43,500
Come on, don't be ridiculous.

118
00:07:45,060 --> 00:07:46,560
It's just a personal hobby.

119
00:07:47,900 --> 00:07:50,800
Just as expected of the Chief,
such keen insight.

120
00:07:56,980 --> 00:07:58,800
Wow, as expected of you, senior.

121
00:07:58,800 --> 00:08:02,380
You made not just the skeleton
but the skin around it too?

122
00:08:03,920 --> 00:08:05,400
Well? Isn't it amazing?

123
00:08:05,400 --> 00:08:09,380
Once that Brontosaurus is finished,
we can open.

124
00:08:09,380 --> 00:08:12,280
Wow, this has more impact
than our dinosaur exhibition.

125
00:08:12,280 --> 00:08:14,180
After all, it cost a lot of money.

126
00:08:15,060 --> 00:08:17,080
We teamed up with a
modeling studio to make it.

127
00:08:17,080 --> 00:08:18,460
You, who can't even pay your resident tax...

128
00:08:18,460 --> 00:08:20,300
How on earth did you come
up with that kind of money?

129
00:08:20,300 --> 00:08:23,000
No, it's all borrowed money.

130
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:25,940
It's all so I can see
the children's happy faces.

131
00:08:25,940 --> 00:08:29,320
And with the admission fees just breaking even,
there's no profit at all.

132
00:08:29,740 --> 00:08:32,560
Still, it looks just like the real thing.

133
00:08:32,560 --> 00:08:34,520
It's surprisingly light for how it looks.

134
00:08:34,520 --> 00:08:35,960
It's hollow inside, after all.

135
00:08:35,960 --> 00:08:36,620
I see.

136
00:08:38,700 --> 00:08:41,900
I made a metal mold based on the
plaster mold we took the other day.

137
00:08:41,900 --> 00:08:44,080
With a metal mold,
we can make them just like taiyaki,

138
00:08:45,060 --> 00:08:53,840
mass-produce them, sell them everywhere, and rake in the profits.
Just like you'd expect from a senior officer! Listen, don't tell the Chief about this.

139
00:08:53,840 --> 00:09:01,240
Yeah, yeah, what are you talking about?
Never mind. Anyway, Chief, look down here.

140
00:09:01,980 --> 00:09:11,520
It has wheels on the legs, so it can be moved when used widely.
I see, you've thought of everything. I can do it too when I put my mind to it.

141
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:13,340
Hey! Ryo-san!

142
00:09:13,800 --> 00:09:14,865
Ryo-san!

143
00:09:14,915 --> 00:09:18,740
Orders are pouring in from all over the country!
We're over ten million yen in the black!

144
00:09:19,100 --> 00:09:19,980
Heave!

145
00:09:20,240 --> 00:09:22,078
This guy's weak with numbers,

146
00:09:22,128 --> 00:09:24,910
and he's gotten some
kind of idea in his head.

147
00:09:24,960 --> 00:09:26,660
What a troublesome guy.

148
00:09:27,380 --> 00:09:29,540
Pay your metropolitan resident tax already.

149
00:09:29,680 --> 00:09:31,120
Ah, no yes.

150
00:09:35,140 --> 00:09:39,700
Just watch. I'll take orders from all
over the world and rake in the money,

151
00:09:39,700 --> 00:09:44,280
whether it's metropolitan tax, ward tax, or
any other tax, don't you dare underestimate me.

152
00:09:44,280 --> 00:09:46,200
I'll pay it all off in one big bang!

153
00:09:52,940 --> 00:09:58,700
Typhoon No. 55, an unseasonable storm, is gradually
heading northeast and approaching the Kanto region,

154
00:09:58,700 --> 00:10:00,640
so please take full precautions.

155
00:10:01,120 --> 00:10:02,660
No wonder the wind is so strong.

156
00:10:02,660 --> 00:10:05,080
Ugh, a typhoon at a time like this.

157
00:10:05,080 --> 00:10:06,920
If it makes landfall, that'll be bad.

158
00:10:06,920 --> 00:10:08,960
Alright, I'm going out for a bit.

159
00:10:08,960 --> 00:10:11,580
You're going on patrol in this wind?

160
00:10:11,580 --> 00:10:14,220
I'm just going to check on the dinosaurs.

161
00:10:14,220 --> 00:10:17,020
If they fall over and break,
we'll take a huge loss.

162
00:10:19,380 --> 00:10:21,960
You're really careful when money's involved,
aren't you?

163
00:10:21,960 --> 00:10:22,480
Seriously.

164
00:10:24,600 --> 00:10:26,880
I'm not losing to a typhoon!

165
00:10:27,400 --> 00:10:29,760
Damn it.

166
00:10:33,120 --> 00:10:33,900
Nnnnngh...

167
00:10:42,320 --> 00:10:43,300
Ryo-san.

168
00:10:43,300 --> 00:10:44,560
You two came too?

169
00:10:44,560 --> 00:10:47,900
Yeah, with this wind,
I'm worried about the dinosaurs.

170
00:10:47,900 --> 00:10:49,040
Alright, let's hurry.

171
00:11:00,840 --> 00:11:02,220
Whoa, no good!

172
00:11:21,940 --> 00:11:23,380
Ryo-san!

173
00:11:26,200 --> 00:11:27,500
What!

174
00:11:30,320 --> 00:11:31,660
It really flew off!

175
00:11:33,720 --> 00:11:34,820
No, it's the same!

176
00:11:35,960 --> 00:11:39,320
I never expected it to actually fly.
My design is pretty impressive!

177
00:11:39,680 --> 00:11:43,280
It must be because we hollowed
out the bones to cut costs.

178
00:11:43,760 --> 00:11:47,540
Alright, since it's come to this, I'm
raising the price of the Pteranodon replica!

179
00:11:49,060 --> 00:11:51,960
No, no, no,
this is no time for that kind of talk!

180
00:11:56,480 --> 00:11:58,860
Uh-oh! This has turned into a disaster!

181
00:12:36,020 --> 00:12:37,800
It's like a monster movie!

182
00:12:44,240 --> 00:12:46,220
This is Odaiba, Tokyo.

183
00:12:46,220 --> 00:12:50,060
Typhoon No.
55, which has been approaching Tokyo Bay,

184
00:12:50,060 --> 00:12:52,120
has grown even stronger.

185
00:12:54,060 --> 00:12:56,220
Cameraman, why are you backing away?

186
00:12:56,400 --> 00:12:57,060
Behind you!

187
00:13:02,520 --> 00:13:05,280
I don't know, but it's not a typhoon,
a dinosaur has come ashore!

188
00:13:10,460 --> 00:13:11,300
This is terrible!

189
00:13:12,380 --> 00:13:13,060
What is it?

190
00:13:13,360 --> 00:13:16,520
A dinosaur has appeared,
and the city is in a state of panic.

191
00:13:16,640 --> 00:13:18,120
What? A dinosaur?

192
00:13:22,400 --> 00:13:24,380
S-s-sorry!

193
00:13:25,040 --> 00:13:27,680
I-I came to pay my resident tax!

194
00:13:30,340 --> 00:13:32,600
Because of the strong
winds from this typhoon,

195
00:13:32,600 --> 00:13:35,560
the dinosaurs from the Sumida Ward
dinosaur park have been blown away,

196
00:13:35,560 --> 00:13:38,340
running wild across the city
and causing damage everywhere.

197
00:13:39,480 --> 00:13:41,900
They're causing trouble all over Tokyo.

198
00:13:41,900 --> 00:13:43,420
What did Ryotsu do?

199
00:13:43,420 --> 00:13:46,680
Apparently he rode a Pteranodon and crashed
into the Metropolitan Government Building.

200
00:13:46,680 --> 00:13:49,540
Honestly,
he went and built something outrageous.

201
00:13:52,740 --> 00:13:55,660
A Tyrannosaurus smashed our roof!

202
00:13:55,660 --> 00:13:57,220
Ours was a concrete block wall!

203
00:13:57,220 --> 00:13:57,960
Answer me!

204
00:13:57,960 --> 00:14:00,600
It's an act of God, due to the typhoon.

205
00:14:00,600 --> 00:14:02,140
You two must have cooked this up together,
didn't you?

206
00:14:02,140 --> 00:14:03,260
Bring out the president!

207
00:14:05,140 --> 00:14:06,820
The president isn't here.

208
00:14:07,240 --> 00:14:08,880
I won't accept just paying damages!

209
00:14:08,880 --> 00:14:11,320
Bring the president here right now!

210
00:14:14,020 --> 00:14:15,720
Ryo-san, we're in trouble!

211
00:14:15,720 --> 00:14:17,900
At this rate, we're going bankrupt!

212
00:14:17,900 --> 00:14:19,820
Orders came in from all over the country,

213
00:14:19,820 --> 00:14:21,680
and we were ten million in the black, right?

214
00:14:22,660 --> 00:14:25,340
But after this incident,
they've all cancelled.

215
00:14:25,340 --> 00:14:27,460
Come on, there must still be a way.

216
00:14:27,460 --> 00:14:30,480
If we get orders from around the world,
we'll be fine.

217
00:14:30,480 --> 00:14:32,900
We can't afford to be
so leisurely about this!

218
00:14:33,260 --> 00:14:35,360
Debt collectors are showing up at my house!

219
00:14:35,360 --> 00:14:37,240
Ryo-san, please do something!

220
00:14:37,600 --> 00:14:41,260
It couldn't be helped.
A typhoon was something we didn't plan for.

221
00:14:42,820 --> 00:14:46,040
We promised to split the losses in half if we ended up in the red,
didn't we?

222
00:14:47,760 --> 00:14:48,880
What's with the sudden...?

223
00:14:49,240 --> 00:14:50,420
Look at this!

224
00:14:50,420 --> 00:14:54,371
A major end-of-century discovery?
A living dinosaur?

225
00:14:54,421 --> 00:14:57,280
Footprints of a dinosaur discovered?
Surprise, surprise!

226
00:14:57,660 --> 00:15:03,580
This is hogwash, just like Nessie of Loch Ness,
Kusshie of Lake Kussharo, or Issie of Lake Ikeda.

227
00:15:03,580 --> 00:15:11,620
Look closer. Nessie only made headlines from blurry photos, but this one's different.
There are footprints, and it's clearly visible in the photo.

228
00:15:12,280 --> 00:15:15,140
Even if it's real,
what does it have to do with me?

229
00:15:15,140 --> 00:15:17,920
I'm going to go catch this dinosaur.

230
00:15:18,460 --> 00:15:21,060
If we capture a real dinosaur alive,

231
00:15:21,540 --> 00:15:23,840
we'll become rich overnight!

232
00:15:24,520 --> 00:15:25,780
Even if we just put it on display,

233
00:15:25,780 --> 00:15:29,140
it'll be as popular as the
first pandas that came to Japan.

234
00:15:29,580 --> 00:15:33,440
Then we train it to perform and
make it the star of the circus.

235
00:15:33,440 --> 00:15:35,800
Can't you train a dinosaur to do tricks?

236
00:15:35,800 --> 00:15:37,220
What are you talking about?

237
00:15:37,220 --> 00:15:39,060
Even Godzilla died, you know!

238
00:15:39,060 --> 00:15:40,560
I don't know about that.

239
00:15:40,560 --> 00:15:42,760
It's the one called Destroy All Monsters!

240
00:15:42,760 --> 00:15:43,860
You don't know it?

241
00:15:43,860 --> 00:15:45,980
It's a movie story, obviously!

242
00:15:47,920 --> 00:15:49,180
There's no such word as "impossible."

243
00:15:49,180 --> 00:15:54,300
In the end, we'll use current genetic
engineering to multiply the dinosaurs

244
00:15:54,820 --> 00:15:58,220
and build a dinosaur park
on par with Jurassic Park.

245
00:15:58,220 --> 00:16:01,680
I'll be the richest man in the world!

246
00:16:10,940 --> 00:16:13,700
Senpai, are you seriously
planning to look for the dinosaur?

247
00:16:13,700 --> 00:16:15,480
Seriously? Hell yeah, I am.

248
00:16:15,480 --> 00:16:18,820
I'm up to my neck in debt.

249
00:16:19,280 --> 00:16:21,940
This is our only chance to strike it rich.

250
00:16:21,940 --> 00:16:25,140
Don't drag me along on your idiotic scheme!

251
00:16:25,140 --> 00:16:28,280
Senpai, I can see the Odoroki
Momo no Ki coming into view.

252
00:16:35,920 --> 00:16:40,300
Senpai, this place looks more like a
tourist spot than an island with dinosaurs.

253
00:16:40,980 --> 00:16:44,660
Then, senpai, let me know when
you've captured the dinosaur alive.

254
00:16:45,480 --> 00:16:51,720
Will you come? The dinosaur's enormous, so when you come to pick us up, bring a big boat.
Got it.

255
00:16:55,480 --> 00:17:00,220
I'll be waiting!
Not that I'm bothered at all.

256
00:17:00,220 --> 00:17:08,740
Alright, I'm going to capture it alive no matter what!
Honda, since we're here, let's hit the beach, chat up some bus girls, and grab a cola at the bar.

257
00:17:09,740 --> 00:17:12,660
We didn't come here for sightseeing!
We came to catch a dinosaur!

258
00:17:13,580 --> 00:17:14,280
Come on, let's go!

259
00:17:14,460 --> 00:17:15,000
R-right.

260
00:17:21,560 --> 00:17:23,780
This is getting kind of creepy.

261
00:17:23,980 --> 00:17:26,240
Well? Doesn't it have atmosphere now?

262
00:17:26,960 --> 00:17:29,380
What's with that crowd of people?

263
00:17:30,360 --> 00:17:33,740
Oh no, don't tell me someone's
already caught the dinosaur?

264
00:17:35,740 --> 00:17:37,800
You may not go any further!

265
00:17:39,740 --> 00:17:41,560
They're the island's residents.

266
00:17:41,560 --> 00:17:43,180
Are you Japanese?

267
00:17:43,180 --> 00:17:45,720
The jungle is a sacred place on this island,

268
00:17:45,720 --> 00:17:48,720
so they're blocking us,
saying humans aren't allowed in.

269
00:17:48,720 --> 00:17:49,360
What did you say?

270
00:17:50,000 --> 00:17:50,920
No way, that's ridiculous.

271
00:17:50,920 --> 00:17:54,000
We came all the way from
Japan to catch a dinosaur!

272
00:17:54,000 --> 00:17:56,480
We're going in, no matter what.

273
00:17:56,480 --> 00:17:57,300
Senpai.

274
00:17:57,880 --> 00:17:58,900
Wait!

275
00:17:58,900 --> 00:17:59,780
Shut up.

276
00:18:00,500 --> 00:18:01,640
Let go!

277
00:18:01,640 --> 00:18:03,900
What are you doing?

278
00:18:03,900 --> 00:18:07,620
Let go, let go!

279
00:18:07,620 --> 00:18:08,940
Senpai!

280
00:18:10,780 --> 00:18:13,260
What's this rumbling? Is it a dinosaur?

281
00:18:13,980 --> 00:18:16,160
Make way for our Queen!

282
00:18:16,160 --> 00:18:17,240
It's the Queen.

283
00:18:17,820 --> 00:18:18,840
Everyone, make way!

284
00:18:18,840 --> 00:18:19,400
Move, move!

285
00:18:19,400 --> 00:18:19,980
Morning!

286
00:18:19,980 --> 00:18:20,760
Morning!

287
00:18:20,760 --> 00:18:21,020
What?

288
00:18:23,840 --> 00:18:24,280
What is it?

289
00:18:28,400 --> 00:18:30,800
Listen in amazement,
and remember what you see!

290
00:18:30,800 --> 00:18:34,560
I am Onoroke-hime, the lady of this island!

291
00:18:34,560 --> 00:18:36,160
Onoroke-hime!

292
00:18:36,160 --> 00:18:37,920
Are you two relatives of Onoroke-hime?

293
00:18:39,920 --> 00:18:43,300
You will surely incur the wrath
of the Yashima guardian deity.

294
00:18:43,800 --> 00:18:45,460
You must never enter!

295
00:18:46,060 --> 00:18:47,260
Guardian deity?

296
00:18:47,720 --> 00:18:50,400
It's the Bikkuri Dokkiri
Ottamagetta Nusshī-sama!

297
00:18:51,200 --> 00:18:53,500
Bikkuri, jake-rin-whatsit Nusshī?

298
00:18:53,880 --> 00:18:55,340
For short, it's just Nusshī-sama.

299
00:18:56,400 --> 00:18:58,260
If you're gonna shorten it,
just say so from the start.

300
00:18:59,180 --> 00:19:01,660
So, what exactly is this Nusshī-sama thing?

301
00:19:02,540 --> 00:19:05,740
Apparently,
it's the dinosaur we're looking for.

302
00:19:06,080 --> 00:19:08,280
I see, so the dinosaurs really do exist!

303
00:19:09,740 --> 00:19:11,140
Now I'm even more fired up!

304
00:19:11,820 --> 00:19:14,040
Did you not hear my words?

305
00:19:14,400 --> 00:19:18,260
Not even the islanders who entered
this jungle have ever returned safely.

306
00:19:18,760 --> 00:19:22,600
Give up on hunting dinosaurs and
enjoy a vacation on this island!

307
00:19:23,020 --> 00:19:24,300
The Onoroke Sisters!

308
00:19:36,420 --> 00:19:40,560
Forget the dinosaur,
let's enjoy island life with us!

309
00:19:41,120 --> 00:19:44,620
We work at Hotel Odoroki Momonoki.

310
00:19:45,680 --> 00:19:46,840
Come stay with us!

311
00:19:48,360 --> 00:19:50,880
Now, everyone, let's dance together!

312
00:19:52,720 --> 00:19:53,780
Oi, oi, oi!

313
00:19:54,300 --> 00:19:56,360
Look at you, getting all googly-eyed.

314
00:19:56,360 --> 00:19:57,200
We don't need you!

315
00:19:57,200 --> 00:19:58,500
It's just us!

316
00:19:58,500 --> 00:20:00,140
Let's go look for the dinosaur!

317
00:20:00,140 --> 00:20:01,060
Hehehe.

318
00:20:01,480 --> 00:20:02,940
The Onoroke Brothers!

319
00:20:02,940 --> 00:20:05,260
Nn-hoh, nn-hoh!

320
00:20:05,260 --> 00:20:07,060
Nn-hoh, nn-hoh!

321
00:20:07,760 --> 00:20:10,020
Nn-hoh, nn-hoh!

322
00:20:10,020 --> 00:20:11,020
Nn-hoh, nn-hoh!

323
00:20:11,920 --> 00:20:13,620
Wonder of wonders, peach tree and prickly ash,
people are our specialty!

324
00:20:13,620 --> 00:20:16,800
Would you like some dinosaur
manju or dinosaur senbei?

325
00:20:17,400 --> 00:20:18,900
For everyone who makes a purchase,

326
00:20:18,900 --> 00:20:21,760
you can watch the most beautiful
sunset in the world with us.

327
00:20:21,760 --> 00:20:23,360
That's a special bonus too!

328
00:20:27,460 --> 00:20:29,420
Why don't you take all of me?

329
00:20:29,420 --> 00:20:30,940
I'm the representative of Dinosaur Manju.

330
00:20:30,940 --> 00:20:32,140
Hey, don't you have a stamp card?

331
00:20:32,740 --> 00:20:33,360
Thank you for your business!

332
00:20:34,220 --> 00:20:37,360
Honestly,
what on earth are all these people here for?

333
00:20:37,820 --> 00:20:40,760
Alright, everyone, now it's showtime!

334
00:20:44,180 --> 00:20:45,600
Is that Kaipan Day?

335
00:20:51,700 --> 00:20:53,080
Hey, Kaipan Deka?

336
00:20:54,300 --> 00:20:57,240
It's Ryotsu! Long time no see.

337
00:20:57,560 --> 00:20:59,940
What are you doing in a place like this?

338
00:21:00,300 --> 00:21:04,740
I'm here on vacation with Dolphin Deka, Gekko Deka
and the others from the Special Crimes Division, but

339
00:21:04,840 --> 00:21:07,920
I was bored,
so they let me join the Onoroke Brothers.

340
00:21:08,240 --> 00:21:10,640
Figures those guys are here too.

341
00:21:10,640 --> 00:21:12,960
More importantly, why are you here?

342
00:21:13,260 --> 00:21:15,160
Obviously, I'm searching for the dinosaur!

343
00:21:15,460 --> 00:21:18,500
Unlike you idlers on vacation, I'm busy.

344
00:21:18,700 --> 00:21:19,540
Let's go, Honda.

345
00:21:19,700 --> 00:21:20,300
Yes.

346
00:21:20,520 --> 00:21:20,920
See ya.

347
00:21:22,340 --> 00:21:23,280
Wait, Ryotsu.

348
00:21:24,300 --> 00:21:26,060
Meeting here must be fate.

349
00:21:27,480 --> 00:21:28,680
Take this with you.

350
00:21:28,680 --> 00:21:30,080
What's this?

351
00:21:30,080 --> 00:21:32,960
Here, Gaida, if anything happens,
wipe with this.

352
00:21:32,960 --> 00:21:34,320
I'll rush over anywhere.

353
00:21:34,320 --> 00:21:35,080
No, it's fine.

354
00:21:35,080 --> 00:21:36,540
Don't hold back.

355
00:21:36,540 --> 00:21:38,480
I'm not holding back, damn it.

356
00:21:38,480 --> 00:21:39,000
See you.

357
00:21:39,600 --> 00:21:41,220
Hey, everyone, sorry to keep you waiting.

358
00:21:41,220 --> 00:21:42,900
Do that last bit again.

359
00:21:45,120 --> 00:21:47,680
Shit, who'd wipe with this junk?

360
00:21:49,080 --> 00:21:53,580
Hey, Senpai, you never know what
might happen with a dinosaur.

361
00:21:53,580 --> 00:21:55,600
Isn't it better to keep it on you?

362
00:21:56,060 --> 00:21:58,140
You hold onto it. Let's go.

363
00:21:58,520 --> 00:21:58,880
Yes.

364
00:21:59,700 --> 00:22:00,840
Hey, Princess.

365
00:22:00,840 --> 00:22:02,600
We don't have money to waste on play,

366
00:22:02,600 --> 00:22:04,520
so we're going to go hunt for the dinosaur.

367
00:22:05,660 --> 00:22:06,620
Hey, wait!

368
00:22:06,620 --> 00:22:07,640
Owner.

369
00:22:08,080 --> 00:22:09,320
Princess Onoroke.

370
00:22:09,320 --> 00:22:10,280
Well, fine.

371
00:22:10,640 --> 00:22:12,460
Once you know how terrifying the jungle is,

372
00:22:12,460 --> 00:22:14,480
you'll give up right away
and come crawling back.

373
00:22:22,340 --> 00:22:26,140
Senpai, I'm not just creeped out anymore,
I'm getting scared.

374
00:22:26,140 --> 00:22:28,820
What are you babbling about? Pull yourself together,
you pathetic coward for a man!

375
00:22:30,740 --> 00:22:32,400
Let's turn back.

376
00:22:32,400 --> 00:22:36,000
Let go of me.
You're hopeless, you know that?

377
00:22:36,700 --> 00:22:38,760
Anyway, I'm starving.

378
00:22:40,160 --> 00:22:42,580
Something smells like food!

379
00:22:42,580 --> 00:22:43,000
You're right.

380
00:22:46,100 --> 00:22:47,560
It's beyond this thicket.

381
00:22:52,320 --> 00:22:53,320
It's food!

382
00:22:53,960 --> 00:22:55,400
Honda, look, look!

383
00:22:55,400 --> 00:22:56,960
What's that? What is this?

384
00:22:56,960 --> 00:23:02,060
There must be other parties that came into
this jungle looking for the dinosaur besides us.

385
00:23:02,540 --> 00:23:06,140
That party must've had a
big blowout party right here.

386
00:23:06,140 --> 00:23:08,260
This must be the leftovers from it.

387
00:23:08,260 --> 00:23:09,960
Now's not the time for puns, sir.

388
00:23:09,960 --> 00:23:12,860
Senpai, this is way too unnatural.

389
00:23:14,600 --> 00:23:15,880
It's called a trap.

390
00:23:15,880 --> 00:23:16,260
A trap?

391
00:23:16,460 --> 00:23:16,920
Not so fast.

392
00:23:16,920 --> 00:23:20,300
You idiot!

393
00:23:20,300 --> 00:23:23,400
If you thought it was a trap,
why didn't you say so sooner?

394
00:23:23,400 --> 00:23:24,640
Sorry.

395
00:23:25,200 --> 00:23:26,220
Senpai, look!

396
00:23:26,920 --> 00:23:27,320
Hey.

397
00:23:28,200 --> 00:23:30,500
So you two got caught in the trap too?

398
00:23:32,500 --> 00:23:35,600
Who on earth would do something like this?

399
00:23:36,760 --> 00:23:39,780
Only a fool would fall
for such a simple trap.

400
00:23:40,820 --> 00:23:42,520
It's the Bookshelf Old Man!

401
00:23:45,320 --> 00:23:48,120
Don't tell me you came
looking for the dinosaur too?

402
00:23:49,680 --> 00:23:52,510
That's right! I'll train the
dinosaur with my bookshelf originals,

403
00:23:52,560 --> 00:23:54,720
and use it as a crowd-pulling panda!

404
00:23:55,320 --> 00:23:58,080
Your thinking is exactly
the same as the senior's.

405
00:23:58,320 --> 00:24:04,180
Shut up! Hey! Bookshelf Old Man! No dinosaur
is going to memorize such filthy originals!

406
00:24:04,740 --> 00:24:08,420
If it doesn't work, we'll just sell
it off to a circus and make a fortune!

407
00:24:08,720 --> 00:24:09,640
See, same thing.

408
00:24:09,640 --> 00:24:12,060
Ugh, put me down.

409
00:24:12,240 --> 00:24:14,980
No, there wasn't.
I'll catch the dinosaur myself.

410
00:24:18,000 --> 00:24:18,680
Damn it.

411
00:24:23,800 --> 00:24:27,460
Useless, useless. That net is made of
steel that can't be cut even with a knife.

412
00:24:27,720 --> 00:24:29,780
The dinosaur will be ours. Farewell.

413
00:24:30,480 --> 00:24:30,920
Let's go.

414
00:24:31,020 --> 00:24:31,660
Right.

415
00:24:32,900 --> 00:24:36,720
Damn you. Bookshelf old man, just you wait.

416
00:24:37,280 --> 00:24:39,040
You seem to be having quite a hard time,
don't you?

417
00:24:39,940 --> 00:24:41,920
How about I help you?

418
00:24:42,460 --> 00:24:43,840
Please do.

419
00:24:43,840 --> 00:24:46,640
The rescue fee is 50,000 yen per person.

420
00:24:47,360 --> 00:24:49,040
What, 50,000 yen?

421
00:24:49,040 --> 00:24:51,220
Cash up front, please.

422
00:24:51,760 --> 00:24:55,500
Don't mess with me! Don't you dare
profit off people's weaknesses!

423
00:24:55,500 --> 00:24:58,160
Hey, we'll pay, so just get us out!

424
00:24:58,160 --> 00:24:58,500
What?

425
00:24:58,500 --> 00:25:02,740
Alright, that's four of you,
so it comes to 200,000 yen.

426
00:25:02,740 --> 00:25:04,580
There's no helping it here, I suppose.

427
00:25:04,580 --> 00:25:05,720
Here's my share.

428
00:25:06,200 --> 00:25:06,680
Here you go.

429
00:25:07,980 --> 00:25:10,960
Onoroke-hime, we've received 200,000 yen.

430
00:25:10,960 --> 00:25:12,540
Alright, I'll cut you free.

431
00:25:12,540 --> 00:25:13,260
There you go.

432
00:25:18,700 --> 00:25:20,040
Us too, please.

433
00:25:20,600 --> 00:25:22,980
We'll pay too.

434
00:25:22,980 --> 00:25:26,540
Smiles included.

435
00:25:29,640 --> 00:25:32,260
Senpai, we don't have 100,000 yen.

436
00:25:32,260 --> 00:25:34,660
Are we going to stay like this forever?

437
00:25:36,720 --> 00:25:39,480
I'll get you for this!
Honda, point your backpack over here!

438
00:25:40,260 --> 00:25:40,800
Like this?

439
00:25:41,040 --> 00:25:42,060
Okay, yeah, that's good.

440
00:25:42,780 --> 00:25:43,820
Yeah, is this good?

441
00:25:43,920 --> 00:25:44,380
Alright, good.

442
00:25:44,440 --> 00:25:45,900
What are you putting together?

443
00:25:45,940 --> 00:25:48,480
It's the long-reach pruning shears I bought
from a mail-order catalog the other day.

444
00:25:48,680 --> 00:25:50,060
Long-reach pruning shears.

445
00:25:50,060 --> 00:25:51,100
Okay, it's done!

446
00:25:52,780 --> 00:25:54,640
With these, even high branches are a breeze.

447
00:25:56,620 --> 00:25:56,940
Hey!

448
00:25:59,660 --> 00:26:03,340
Hey, how about this?
I won't pay you two a single red cent.

449
00:26:03,340 --> 00:26:04,360
Let's go, Honda!

450
00:26:04,360 --> 00:26:08,800
That gorilla guy's not bad, is he?

451
00:26:09,300 --> 00:26:12,160
Honda, don't let
Hondaragoyaji beat us to it!

452
00:26:12,160 --> 00:26:16,880
Hondaragoyaji,
I'll make sure you pay for this!

